From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:31:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: a static sample mask with every sample is not lowered

A fragment shader of a pipeline whose static sample mask has a bit for
every rasterization sample is no longer given the sample mask output
and KK_WORKAROUND_7's discard. DXVK gives the mask as
sampleMask & ((1 << samples) - 1), 0x1 at one sample, which the check
against UINT16_MAX took for a partial mask: every whole pipeline that
DXVK built at one sample read the sample mask and could discard. Such a
mask masks nothing. A mask without some sample is lowered as before.

This is the comparison mesa 0100 made for MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=gpl's
separate links, on the path that runs without it.

Linear: PLA-430
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-22-kk-gpl-cold-cache.md
Offered-upstream: not yet
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index 83332c1..411e265 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -703,8 +703,12 @@ kk_lower_fs(struct kk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir,
 
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, msl_nir_fs_io_types);
 
+   /* Playport (PLA-430): a mask that has every rasterization sample, as
+    * DXVK's 0x1 at one sample, masks nothing. */
    if (!gpl_separate && state->ms && state->ms->rasterization_samples &&
-       state->ms->sample_mask != UINT16_MAX) {
+       (state->ms->sample_mask &
+        BITFIELD_MASK(state->ms->rasterization_samples)) !=
+          BITFIELD_MASK(state->ms->rasterization_samples)) {
 
       /* KK_WORKAROUND_7 */
       if (!(pdev->settings.disabled_workarounds & BITFIELD64_BIT(7))) {
